# ─── OCHI booking wiring ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Two layers:

# 1) CLIENT — none needed. The browser always POSTs same-origin /api/book (a
#    constant in lib/booking.ts, not an env read — the old build-time
#    NEXT_PUBLIC_SECRETARY_BOOKING_URL was never set in any published image, so
#    production permanently stubbed success; audit 2026-08-04). The only client
#    knob is the explicit dev-only stub below, for exercising the confirm →
#    success flow with no backend. Never set it in CI or a Dockerfile.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_STUB=1

# 2) SERVER — the /api/book proxy forwards here with the shared secret.
#    UPSTREAM is Ernest's public lead-intake endpoint; SECRET must match
#    OCHI_BOOKING_SECRET in the ErnestOfGaia deploy. If either is unset the
#    proxy degrades to a soft success and the page's text/email fallbacks
#    remain the real path.
SECRETARY_BOOKING_URL=https://ernestofgaia.xyz/api/ochi-booking
OCHI_BOOKING_SECRET=
